<%# locals: (fresh_key:)

    The one-time plaintext reveal. Fuime stores only ciphertext + last4, so this
    card is the only place the secret is ever rendered. Dismiss removes it from
    the DOM; a later GET of this page cannot reconstruct it.

    The Copy button uses the existing clipboard Stimulus controller (no extra
    logging — that controller writes to the clipboard and nowhere else).

    `data-turbo-temporary` is on the card, not the `#fuime-fresh-api-key`
    wrapper: Turbo strips temporary nodes before it snapshots. If the wrapper
    went too, a later create stream would have no target. The card going is
    what we want — a back-navigation snapshot must not restore the secret. %>
<div class="card mb2" data-fuime-fresh-key data-turbo-temporary style="border-color: var(--success);">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">Your new key</h2>
  <p class="muted text-sm">
    Copy it now. This is the only time it will be shown — Fuime keeps only an
    encrypted copy and cannot show it to you again.
  </p>
  <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start gap-2 mt1">
    <pre class="m0" style="overflow-x: auto;"><code><%= fresh_key %></code></pre>
    <button type="button"
            class="btn shrink-0"
            data-controller="clipboard"
            data-clipboard-text-value="<%= fresh_key %>"
            data-clipboard-confirm-text-value="Copied!"
            data-action="clipboard#copy">
      Copy
    </button>
  </div>
  <p class="mt1">
    <button type="button"
            class="btn"
            onclick="this.closest('[data-fuime-fresh-key]').remove()">
      I've copied it
    </button>
  </p>
</div>
